-From: GSL CI Matrix Enhancement
-Date: Fri, 13 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH 4.7.5] Unified CI matrix with include blocks, Sphinx typehints
- config, FetchContent GIT_SHALLOW
-
-This patch introduces the following changes:
-
-1. New .github/workflows/ci.yml -- Unified Matrix Strategy
-   - Single `build-and-test` job with `include`-driven matrix covering:
-     * GCC 12, 13, 14      (ubuntu-latest)
-     * Clang 16, 17, 18    (ubuntu-latest)
-     * XCode 14.3.1, 15.4  (macos-13 / macos-14) via DEVELOPER_DIR
-     * VS2019 MSVC + LLVM ClangCL  (windows-2019)
-     * VS2022 MSVC + LLVM ClangCL  (windows-2022)
-   - CC/CXX explicitly set via matrix variables → job-level `env:`.
-   - XCode DEVELOPER_DIR toggled per-entry; `xcode-select` used as
-     secondary fallback in the dedicated step.
-   - Windows toolchain selection via `-T ClangCL` for LLVM entries.
-   - `exclude` block with flag variables for known incompatibilities
-     (GCC 12 + C++20/23, Clang 17 + C++23).
-   - `fail-fast: false` so independent compiler issues don't cancel
-     the entire matrix run.
-
-2. New docs/conf.py -- Sphinx Configuration
-   - Full explanation and resolution of return-type duplication
-     caused by simultaneous napoleon_use_rtype=True and
-     typehints_use_rtype=True.
-   - Recommended "code-as-truth" strategy:
-       napoleon_use_rtype      = False
-       typehints_use_rtype     = True
-       typehints_document_rtype = True
-   - ``typehints_fixup_module_name`` mapping for threading.local
-     broken-link fixup.
-
-3. CMakeLists.txt -- FetchContent Documentation
-   - Added comment block documenting the recommended FetchContent
-     usage pattern with GIT_TAG "v4.2.0" and GIT_SHALLOW ON,
-     including rationale for shallow clones in CI environments.
-
-4. tests/CMakeLists.txt.in -- GIT_SHALLOW ON
-   - Added GIT_SHALLOW ON to ExternalProject_Add(googletest) to
-     speed up CI test dependency downloads.
-
